From: NixKits <https://github.com/Kihara777/NixKits>
Subject: [PATCH] stdenv: migrate stdenv.is<Platform> to stdenv.hostPlatform.is<Platform>

nixpkgs 2026-05-09 deprecated the short-form platform predicates on
`stdenv` (isLinux, isDarwin, isx86_64, …) in favour of the canonical
`stdenv.hostPlatform.*`. nixpkgs keeps them as warning aliases gated by
`config.allowAliases` (pkgs/stdenv/generic/default.nix:205-212):

    lib.mapAttrs
      (name: value:
        lib.warn "stdenv.${name} is deprecated, use stdenv.hostPlatform.${name} instead" value)
      { inherit (hostPlatform) isLinux isDarwin isx86_64 …; }

Reading the old names therefore prints a warning on every evaluation.
Because this flake's overlay is evaluated for `nixpkgs.overlays`, the
warning surfaced in *any* downstream NixOS build that uses it —
including builds that never touch ComfyUI:

    evaluation warning: stdenv.isLinux is deprecated, use stdenv.hostPlatform.isLinux instead
    evaluation warning: stdenv.isx86_64 is deprecated, use stdenv.hostPlatform.isx86_64 instead

Migrate all 44 occurrences (36 in the flake + nix/, plus the vendored
package definitions) to the canonical form. This is a mechanical,
behaviour-preserving rename: `stdenv.isLinux` is literally the same
value as `stdenv.hostPlatform.isLinux`.

Note `config.allowAliases = false` is *not* a workaround: it removes the
aliases entirely and breaks evaluation here and in downstream configs
that still use aliased package names (e.g. `nettools`).

Base revision: 01ef7aa (fix: doCheck=false …)
